Both movers are NO_MODE with zero credited bits at the anchor. All four evaluations pass the unchanged guard, with served counts 3/3/4/4 in both views. Source users 2–4 are the three served anchor users; the joint serves users 1 and 5–7. The roster remains all eight users, and the positive bit interaction is computed from delivered bits, not from changing service labels.

**Physical cause:** B moves to a beam with enough occupancy to select a transmitted mode; A jointly removes its cochannel interferer. Comparing B-only with joint, B has target **QPSK 3/4** and transmitted **QPSK 1/3 at every boundary in both configurations**. At t=1.28 s, B-only has actual SINR **0.583304757**, below the unchanged QPSK 1/3 threshold **0.926443106**. Joint action raises actual SINR to **1.916345394**, so that transmission decodes. B’s RF power simultaneously drops from 0.857235753 to 0.063714693 W; neither of those transmissions is capped. Seven B boundaries are rescued this way.

Realised Psi contains **+0.255285333 Gb of delivered-bit interaction**, plus **+1.456127417 Gb** from an energy interaction of −73.837582815 J. Thus decoding contributes positively, although the energy contribution is larger. The source-beam occupancy change and B’s departure from its original capped link occur identically in B-only and joint; they do not explain their fixed-mode threshold difference.

An executed physical control changes only X’s reuse colour from 0 to 2. It retains coordinates, antenna gains, assignments, occupancies, stochastic keys and prices, while removing X–Y interference. Psi becomes −0.000005916 bits in both views, negligible floating-point integration residue; both bit and energy interactions also vanish. This isolates interference as necessary for the original coalition interaction.

**Qualification:** B-only already delivers some bits over the full 30.08-s step; “B alone gains nothing” is satisfied as a negative full-score change, not as zero delivered bits at every boundary. The stricter reading requiring B-only never to decode is **not established** by this witness. The joint also has negative Delta F: this example proves positive interaction, not a profitable joint move. The actual fixed-mode decode cliff occurs in the realised view. In the margin view, mode selection uses the same SINR subsequently passed to the decoder, so a selected mode cannot fail its own threshold by construction; its positive Psi here comes from coupled energy saving.

